{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nconst int MOD = 1e9 + 7;\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nstruct Mat {\n    ll a[35][35];\n    Mat() { memset(a, 0, sizeof(a)); }\n    Mat identity(int n) {\n        Mat res;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= n; ++i) res.a[i][i] = 1;\n        return res;\n    }\n};\n\nMat mul(const Mat& x, const Mat& y, int m) {\n    Mat z;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j <= m; ++j) {\n            ll sum = 0;\n            for (int k = 0; k <= m; ++k)\n                sum = (sum + x.a[i][k] * y.a[k][j]) % MOD;\n            z.a[i][j] = sum;\n        }\n    return z;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    ll n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    ll tmp = n;\n    int cnt = -1;\n    ll dig[75];\n    while (tmp) {\n        dig[++cnt] = tmp % m;\n        tmp /= m;\n    }\n    vector<vector<Mat>> f(cnt + 1, vector<Mat>(m));\n    Mat g;\n    g.a[0][m] = 1;\n    for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n        for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i) {\n            f[0][j].a[i][j] = 1;\n            f[0][j].a[i][i] = 1;\n        }\n    }\n    for (int i = 1; i <= cnt; ++i) {\n        vector<Mat> pre(m), suf(m);\n        pre[0] = f[i - 1][0];\n        for (int j = 1; j < m; ++j)\n            pre[j] = mul(pre[j - 1], f[i - 1][j], m);\n        suf[m - 1] = f[i - 1][m - 1];\n        for (int j = m - 2; j >= 0; --j)\n            suf[j] = mul(f[i - 1][j], suf[j + 1], m);\n        f[i][0] = suf[0];\n        for (int j = 1; j < m; ++j)\n            f[i][j] = mul(suf[j], pre[j - 1], m);\n    }\n    int cur = 0;\n    for (int i = cnt; i >= 0; --i) {\n        while (dig[i]--) {\n            g = mul(g, f[i][cur], m);\n            cur = (cur + 1) % m;\n        }\n    }\n    ll ans = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i)\n        ans = (ans + g.a[0][i]) % MOD;\n    cout << ans << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nMOD = 10**9 + 7\n\ndef mul(A, B, m):\n    \"\"\"Multiply two (m+1)x(m+1) matrices modulo MOD.\"\"\"\n    size = m + 1\n    C = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    for i in range(size):\n        for k in range(size):\n            aik = A[i][k]\n            if aik:\n                for j in range(size):\n                    C[i][j] = (C[i][j] + aik * B[k][j]) % MOD\n    return C\n\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    \n    # Handle n == 0 (the original C++ code would crash, but we make it work)\n    if n == 0:\n        print(1)\n        return\n    \n    # Extract digits in base m (least significant first)\n    digits = []\n    tmp = n\n    while tmp:\n        digits.append(tmp % m)\n        tmp //= m\n    cnt = len(digits) - 1  # index of most significant digit\n    \n    # f[i][j] is a matrix of size (m+1) x (m+1)\n    f = [[None] * m for _ in range(cnt + 1)]\n    \n    # Initialize f[0][j]\n    size = m + 1\n    for j in range(m):\n        mat = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n        for i in range(size):\n            mat[i][j] = 1\n            mat[i][i] = 1\n        f[0][j] = mat\n    \n    # Build f[i][j] for i >= 1\n    for i in range(1, cnt + 1):\n        pre = [None] * m\n        suf = [None] * m\n        pre[0] = f[i-1][0]\n        for j in range(1, m):\n            pre[j] = mul(pre[j-1], f[i-1][j], m)\n        suf[m-1] = f[i-1][m-1]\n        for j in range(m-2, -1, -1):\n            suf[j] = mul(f[i-1][j], suf[j+1], m)\n        f[i][0] = suf[0]\n        for j in range(1, m):\n            f[i][j] = mul(suf[j], pre[j-1], m)\n    \n    # Initialize g with a single 1 at (0, m)\n    g = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    g[0][m] = 1\n    \n    cur = 0\n    # Process digits from most significant to least\n    for i in range(cnt, -1, -1):\n        while digits[i] > 0:\n            g = mul(g, f[i][cur], m)\n            cur = (cur + 1) % m\n            digits[i] -= 1\n    \n    ans = sum(g[0][i] for i in range(size)) % MOD\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0005402297829277813, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.00036459474358707666, -0.23228079080581665, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.581423415103927e-05, -0.029784899204969406, -0.0052339909598231316, 0.0, -0.0011701886542141438, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -1.3112935448589269e-05, -3.099436753473128e-06, -0.03823075070977211, -0.0054294029250741005, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0001731960946926847, -1.7165990357170813e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.8401203751564026, -0.17895303666591644, -0.005347116384655237, -0.31625741720199585, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.005675274413079023, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.019788116216659546, 0.0, -0.014380390755832195, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.3156684935092926, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, -